  Actually, Jonathan, I would have dismissed it too, as "oh, great, another
suggestion for a writing system"  But this one was actually different.
 It's suggesting that rather than a simply one-to-one substitution of the
existing orthography to another letter-based system, that we basically give
each brivla a single symbol, based on things such as place value, so that,
for example, each of the danlu gismu might look similar, since they have
similar terbri.   It's an intriguing suggestion, but I doubt there's much
support for it.
             --gejyspa


